{"final":{"answer":"The reserve for product warranties increased by $6 million from 2005 to 2006 (from $4 million to $10 million).","value":6,"unit":"USD_million","sources":["source:q11n3","source:q11n4"],"result_id":"tool:1","explanation":"Source q11 states: 'as of dec. 31, 2006 and 2005, the reserve for product warranties was $10 million and $4 million, respectively.' Change = 2006 reserve ($10M) - 2005 reserve ($4M) = $6 million increase. This is corroborated by the movement components in q12–q14: beginning $4M + pretax charges $4M + $7M assumed in acquisitions - cash outlays $5M = $10M ending reserve."}}